From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 21:20:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 138/225] ASoC: rg-rotate: reconstruct stock speaker path in
 the 7.1 port

The speaker is driven through the codec HP output into an external
AW87391 smart-amp (not the internal SC2730 class-D). After the vendor
port, playback was silent then very quiet because nothing reconstructs
the levels/routing that stock's Android HAL programmed per-stream.

Fold the known-good chain into the driver so no userspace HAL is needed:

- vbc-dai.c: enable the AG IIS0 -> audio-top clock route at codec probe
  (was defaulting to disable at boot, i.e. silent).
- sprd-codec.c: seed DA_IG=3 and HPL/HPR=4 on each DAC/HP power-up. These
  ANA_CDC gain fields are bare analog-domain registers with no shadow and
  cold-start at 0 (-15 dB DAC / muted HP) every stream.
- sprd-codec.c: lift the DAC gain control cap 2 -> 3 (2-bit field; stock
  reached 3 = -12.75 dB).
- aw87390.c: raise the AW87391 PA from 15 dB to 21 dB (max 24 dB).

Speaker now plays cleanly. Known remaining issue: a regularly-timed pop
through sustained tones (per-period/buffer boundary), to be chased next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
